# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# What IS committed, deliberately:
#   session 01/ … session 19/   notebooks + their figures (the course itself)
#   docs/                       the generated site — GitHub Pages serves it from
#                               this folder, so it must stay tracked
#   build.py, website/          the site generator and its stylesheet
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Manuscript — drafts, figures and exports stay local, out of the public site
paper/

# Build notes for the site generator — not part of the published course
BUILDING.md

# Source contributor photos. The build re-encodes these into
# docs/assets/authors/*.webp, which IS committed and is what the site and the
# README display — so a clone needs this folder only to regenerate them.
author images/

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.eggs/
build/
dist/

# Virtual environments
.venv/
venv/
env/
ENV/

# Jupyter
.ipynb_checkpoints/
*/.ipynb_checkpoints/
profile_default/
ipython_config.py

# Datasets — the chest X-ray data is downloaded, never committed
data/
datasets/
chest_xray/
*.zip
*.tar
*.tar.gz
*.h5
*.hdf5

# Trained weights and checkpoints
*.pt
*.pth
*.ckpt
*.onnx
*.pkl
checkpoints/
runs/
lightning_logs/
wandb/

# Editors / IDEs
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
*~

# OS cruft
.DS_Store
._*
.Spotlight-V100
.Trashes
Thumbs.db
ehthumbs.db
desktop.ini

# Local scratch
scratch/
tmp/
*.log
